title A ten-digit decimal read as a git nib
prompt Same lap as 20260916.201904 -- a red surfaced after that work had landed and pushed.
rota none -- the rota was read and recorded in this lap's first log; this is the booking that followed it
think Re-ran nib_honesty after the push, because a floating nib means pushable, rewritten, or withdrawn, and a push should clear it.
think gone=2 did not fall. A count that will not move under its own named cure is measuring something else, so I asked the scan to list.
think It listed 1103515245 and 2147483648 -- the awk LCG multiplier and modulus from Diffuser's own card account, each exactly ten digits.
think advertised_hashes() gathers with grep -oE for ten hex characters, and the digits 0 through 9 are valid hex, so any ten-digit decimal in the card's prose reads as an advertised commit.
think Eleven lines below, the same file reads the living nib BY ITS KEY rather than by shape. The narrow reading and the loose one stand in one file and only the narrow one was ever asked what it was reading.
obs Booked rather than repaired. The lap had landed; the repair wants a ruling on whether an advertised hash is recognised by POSITION or by RESOLUTION, and a decimal that happens to resolve is a different question from one that cannot.
obs The class widens as the card does -- a byte count, a port, a timestamp or any ten-digit measurement written without a separator joins it, and Gauge asks every claim to carry a figure.
obs The refusal is indistinguishable from the ordinary state of a lap whose work is still local, which is why it had stood unread.
obs Also stopped a spent cold endurance run this lap: my own claim push moved HEAD while the roster ran, fixing its verdict at tree_moved. The claim-before-build protocol and the hold-still-while-the-roster-runs protocol collide for any lap that opens an instrument.
loom guard=nib_honesty advertised=3 gone=2 resolving=1 false_positives=2
